{"case_id":"T8016","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point"],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":97,"affected_functions":["xmlParseDocument","xmlParseChunk","xmlSwitchEncodingName","xmlErrMemory","xmlVErrParser"],"reason":"H0 is only shared fuzz-data and allocation/entity-loading support; it defines no fuzz entry point and never invokes parser entry points such as xmlParseDocument or xmlParseChunk. Consequently S1+H0 has a material reachability gap, but the same gap already existed in S0+H0. The commit mainly consolidates parser error/state handling through xmlErrParser, xmlVErrParser, PARSER_STOPPED, and xmlErrMemory, while xmlSwitchEncodingName is also reached internally from existing parser flows such as xmlSetDeclaredEncoding and xmlDoRead. These changes do not materially aggravate H0's pre-existing absence of a parser driver.","evidence":["H0 defines helpers including xmlFuzzDataInit, xmlFuzzReadEntities, xmlFuzzEntityLoader, and xmlFuzzMemSetup, but contains neither LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput nor a call to a production parser entry point.","Both S0 and S1 parser implementations expose parsing through identifiers such as xmlParseDocument and xmlParseChunk, neither of which is called by H0.","S1 routes many existing error paths through xmlErrParser and xmlVErrParser and changes stop-state checks to PARSER_STOPPED(ctxt), indicating an internal error/state refactor rather than a new required harness protocol.","The new xmlSwitchEncodingName function is invoked by existing production paths including xmlSetDeclaredEncoding, xmlCtxtResetPush, xmlDoRead, and xmlParseInNodeContext; it does not make H0's already-total lack of parser invocation materially worse."] ,"recommended_action":"No maintenance is attributable to this commit. Independently, replace or supplement H0 with a target harness that initializes fuzz data and invokes a parser entry point such as xmlParseDocument or xmlParseChunk."}
